#: ../../errors.rst:3
msgid "Error messages"
msgstr "错误信息"

#: ../../errors.rst:6
msgid ""
"A report should name the problem, show its location, and give a useful "
"next step. Guidedog keeps that evidence as structured data. The terminal "
"adds color and a source marker. JSON keeps the data without terminal "
"decoration."
msgstr ""
"诊断报告应说明问题、标明位置，并给出有用的下一步。Guidedog 将这些信息保存为结构化数据。终端显示增加颜色和源码标记；JSON "
"保留数据，不含终端装饰。"

#: ../../errors.rst:10
msgid "Reading a report"
msgstr "如何阅读诊断报告"

#: ../../errors.rst:25
msgid "A report has four parts, always in this order:"
msgstr "报告始终按以下顺序分为四部分："

#: ../../errors.rst:27
msgid "**The title bar.** The title names the kind of problem in capitals. Warnings and notes start with ``WARNING:`` and ``NOTE:``. At the right of the bar is the report's code, such as ``rst.substitution.undefined``: a stable name we can search for."
msgstr "**标题栏。** 标题用大写字母说明问题类型。警告和说明分别以 ``WARNING:`` 和 ``NOTE:`` 开头。标题栏右侧是报告代码，例如 ``rst.substitution.undefined``：这是一个稳定的名称，可以拿来搜索。"

#: ../../errors.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Where.** The file and line, the source line itself, and a marker under "
"the text the problem is about. A problem that is not about one line (a "
"missing folder, a flag) shows only the path, or nothing."
msgstr ""
"**位置。**\\ 显示文件名、行号、源码行，以及问题文本下方的标记。若问题不涉及某一行，如目录缺失或参数错误，只显示路径，或不显示位置。"

#: ../../errors.rst:33
msgid ""
"**What happened.** The explanation, followed, when it matters, by what "
"the problem means for the output: here, that nothing was written."
msgstr "**发生了什么。**\\ 先解释问题；必要时再说明它对输出的影响，例如本次没有写入任何内容。"

#: ../../errors.rst:35
msgid ""
"**What to do.** The hint, in green on a color terminal: a concrete "
"direction. Where there are several ways to fix the problem, the hint "
"names them, the most likely first."
msgstr "**如何处理。**\\ 支持彩色的终端用绿色显示具体建议。如果有多种修复方式，会依次列出，最可能适用的放在前面。"

#: ../../errors.rst:39
msgid "Colors only underline what the words already say. ``--color=never`` turns them off. ``--color=always`` keeps them when the output is not a terminal."
msgstr "颜色只是强调文字已经表达的内容。``--color=never`` 关闭颜色。``--color=always`` 在输出不是终端时也保留颜色。"

#: ../../errors.rst:42
msgid "Every hint gives directions"
msgstr "每条提示都指明下一步"

#: ../../errors.rst:45
msgid "Guidedog holds its own messages to this rule. A hint starts with what to do (\"Add\", \"Pass\", \"Set\", \"Rename\", \"Run\"). It names what to do it to, such as ``--budget=MIB``, ``root_doc`` in ``conf.toml``, or the directive's option. Tests check the messages Guidedog emits. They fail when a hint is empty, repeats the message, or says only \"report this\" without saying what to report with. Two other forms are allowed, because they name the fix themselves. One is a suggestion (\"Did you mean numfig?\"). The other, for a note that needs no action, is \"Nothing to do:\" with the reason."
msgstr "Guidedog 自己的消息也遵守这条规则。提示以要做的动作开头（“Add”“Pass”“Set”“Rename”“Run”），并指明动作的对象，例如 ``--budget=MIB``、``conf.toml`` 中的 ``root_doc``，或指令的选项。测试会检查 Guidedog 发出的消息：提示为空、重复消息内容，或只说“report this”而不说明报告时要附上什么，测试都会失败。另外允许两种形式，因为它们本身就指明了修正方法。一种是建议（“Did you mean numfig?”）。另一种用于无需操作的说明，即“Nothing to do:”加上原因。"

#: ../../errors.rst:52
msgid "When the problem is Guidedog's own fault, the hint says so. It asks us to report it with the command we ran, the input that caused it, and the output of ``guidedog --version``."
msgstr "如果问题出在 Guidedog 自身，提示会明确说明，并请我们附上所运行的命令、导致问题的输入以及 ``guidedog --version`` 的输出来报告。"

#: ../../errors.rst:56
msgid "Reports for programs"
msgstr "供程序读取的报告"

#: ../../errors.rst:59
msgid ""
"``--diagnostics=json`` writes each report as one JSON object per line on "
"standard error, for editors and continuous integration:"
msgstr "``--diagnostics=json`` 将每条报告作为一个 JSON 对象写入标准错误，每行一个，便于编辑器和持续集成读取："

#: ../../errors.rst:70
msgid "(shown wrapped here; each object is on one line). ``schema`` is the version of this format. It changes only when a field does, so a program checks it before reading the rest. Columns count Unicode scalars, not bytes or terminal cells, from 1. ``source`` is the complete original source line. The terminal shows a bounded window around the error. It aligns its caret after escaping controls and measuring wide characters. ``category`` is the warning's category, as ``suppress_warnings`` names it, or empty."
msgstr "（此处折行显示；实际每个对象占一行）。``schema`` 是此格式的版本，只在字段变化时才改变，因此程序应先检查它，再读取其余内容。列号从 1 开始，按 Unicode 标量值计数，而不是按字节或终端单元格。``source`` 是完整的原始源码行。终端只显示错误附近有限的一段，并在转义控制字符、计算宽字符的宽度之后对齐插入符。``category`` 是警告的类别，即 ``suppress_warnings`` 中使用的名称，也可能为空。"

#: ../../errors.rst:77
msgid "When memory runs out"
msgstr "内存不足时"

#: ../../errors.rst:80
msgid "Reaching a bound is a report, not a crash. There are two kinds:"
msgstr "触及上限时会生成报告，而不是崩溃。分为两种情况："

#: ../../errors.rst:82
msgid "``host.budget`` (MEMORY BUDGET REACHED)"
msgstr "``host.budget``\\ （达到内存预算）"

#: ../../errors.rst:83
msgid "The build reached the memory it may hold, its budget (``--budget=MIB``, 1 GiB by default). The budget counts what Guidedog reads and keeps: sources, included files, and the PDF the embedded Typst compiler returns. The report names the step and the file that needed the memory. The hint names a budget that fits, as a number. For example:"
msgstr "构建达到了允许持有的内存，即预算（``--budget=MIB``，默认 1 GiB）。预算统计 Guidedog 读取并保留的内容：源文件、被包含的文件，以及内嵌 Typst 编译器返回的 PDF。报告会指出需要这些内存的步骤和文件。提示会以数字给出一个够用的预算。例如："

#: ../../errors.rst:91
msgid "The number is the larger of two figures. One is what the build held plus four times the refused step (the step also holds its output and the copy it writes). The other is twice the old budget. The number is rounded up to 64 MiB. It is no more than the memory the machine has free, when the step fits there. When it does not, the hint says so:"
msgstr "这个数字取两个值中的较大者：一个是构建已持有的内存加上被拒步骤所需内存的四倍（该步骤还要持有它的输出和它写入的副本），另一个是旧预算的两倍。结果向上取整到 64 MiB。如果该步骤放得进机器的空闲内存，这个数字就不超过空闲内存量。放不下时，提示会明确说明："

#: ../../errors.rst:99
msgid "``GUIDEDOG_AVAILABLE_MIB`` states the machine's free memory when the system's own figure misleads, for example inside a container."
msgstr "当系统自己给出的数字有误导性时（例如在容器内），可以用 ``GUIDEDOG_AVAILABLE_MIB`` 指明机器的空闲内存。"

#: ../../errors.rst:102
msgid "``host.memory`` (OUT OF MEMORY)"
msgstr "``host.memory``\\ （内存不足）"

#: ../../errors.rst:103
msgid "The system could not provide a buffer the budget allowed. The command stops without using it. A build publishes nothing, a GDS change is applied whole or not at all, and ``convert`` writes a whole page or none. Free memory, or build with fewer threads (``-j 1``), and run the command again. Once a build has decided to publish, switching its output into place needs no further planning. So a refusal cannot stop a publication halfway. The next build finishes an interrupted publication."
msgstr "系统无法提供预算所允许的缓冲区。命令停止，不会使用它：构建不发布任何内容，GDS 修改要么整体应用、要么完全不应用，``convert`` 要么写出整页、要么什么都不写。释放内存，或用更少的线程构建（``-j 1``），然后重新运行命令。构建一旦决定发布，把输出切换到位就不再需要额外规划，因此拒绝不会让发布半途而止。被中断的发布会由下一次构建完成。"

#: ../../errors.rst:110
msgid "A document's own size is bounded separately, by ``--max-nodes``, ``--max-depth`` and ``--stack-kib``. An oversized document is reported with the limit it reached. See :doc:`internals/memory` for how the budget and these limits divide the work. The Odin implementation could also keep working memory on disk (``--memory=disk``). The Rust implementation bounds a conversion by its limits instead, so there is no disk mode."
msgstr "文档本身的规模另由 ``--max-nodes``、``--max-depth`` 和 ``--stack-kib`` 限制。超出规模的文档会报告它触及的限制。预算与这些限制如何分工，见 :doc:`internals/memory`。Odin 实现还可以把工作内存放在磁盘上（``--memory=disk``）。Rust 实现则用这些限制约束每次转换，因此没有磁盘模式。"

#: ../../errors.rst:116
msgid "Both end with status 3."
msgstr "两种情况都以状态 3 退出。"

#: ../../errors.rst:118
msgid "Exit status"
msgstr "退出状态"

#: ../../errors.rst:121
msgid ""
"Every command ends with one of these statuses, so scripts can tell kinds "
"of failure apart:"
msgstr "每条命令都以以下状态之一结束，脚本可据此区分失败类型："

#: ../../errors.rst:125
msgid "Status"
msgstr "状态"

#: ../../errors.rst:125
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

#: ../../errors.rst:127
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#: ../../errors.rst:127
msgid "Success. The output was written (and, for a build, published)."
msgstr "成功。输出已写入；若为构建命令，也已发布。"

#: ../../errors.rst:128
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

#: ../../errors.rst:128
msgid ""
"The input has a problem: an error in a document, a policy refusal (raw "
"content without ``--raw``), a document that could not be read, or a "
"warning when ``-W`` or ``--strict`` treats warnings as errors."
msgstr ""
"输入有问题：文档错误、策略拒绝（未使用 ``--raw`` 的原始内容）、文档无法读取，或 ``-W``\\ 、\\ ``--strict`` "
"将警告视为错误。"

#: ../../errors.rst:131
msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

#: ../../errors.rst:131
msgid ""
"The command was used wrongly: an unknown flag or command, a missing or "
"invalid value, or an invalid setting in ``conf.toml`` or ``-D``."
msgstr "命令用法错误：未知参数或命令、缺失或无效的值，或者 ``conf.toml``\\ 、\\ ``-D`` 中的无效设置。"

#: ../../errors.rst:133
msgid "3"
msgstr "3"

#: ../../errors.rst:133
msgid ""
"A limit was reached: the memory budget (``--budget``), the nesting depth "
"(``--max-depth``), the node count (``--max-nodes``), the stack "
"(``--stack-kib``), a source too large, or memory the system could not "
"provide."
msgstr ""
"达到限制：内存预算（\\ ``--budget``\\ ）、嵌套深度（\\ ``--max-depth``\\ ）、节点数（\\ "
"``--max-nodes``\\ ）、栈（\\ ``--stack-kib``\\ ）、源文件过大，或系统无法提供内存。"

#: ../../errors.rst:136
msgid "4"
msgstr "4"

#: ../../errors.rst:136
msgid ""
"A file or an outside program failed: a path that cannot be read or "
"written, a file that changed while it was read, or Typst not starting or "
"not finishing."
msgstr "文件或外部程序失败：路径无法读取或写入、文件读取期间发生变化，或者 Typst 无法启动或完成。"

#: ../../errors.rst:138
msgid "5"
msgstr "5"

#: ../../errors.rst:138
msgid "Guidedog failed internally, and the report asks us to report it."
msgstr "Guidedog 内部出错，报告会请我们提交问题。"

#: ../../errors.rst:139
msgid "70"
msgstr "70"

#: ../../errors.rst:139
msgid "Guidedog crashed. It prints ``GUIDEDOG CRASHED (internal error)`` with the command that ran, the fault, and what ``guidedog --version`` prints, and says where to report it: the issue tracker our build names, or else whoever provided our build. Because builds publish only at the end, a crash leaves the previous output in place."
msgstr "Guidedog 崩溃了。它会打印 ``GUIDEDOG CRASHED (internal error)``，以及所运行的命令、故障和 ``guidedog --version`` 的输出，并说明到哪里报告：我们所用构建版本指定的问题跟踪器，没有的话就是提供该构建版本的人。由于构建只在最后发布，崩溃时之前的输出保持不变。"

#: ../../errors.rst:144
msgid "130"
msgstr "130"

#: ../../errors.rst:144
msgid "The command was interrupted with Ctrl+C. Published files were left unchanged."
msgstr "命令被 Ctrl+C 中断。已发布的文件保持不变。"

#: ../../errors.rst:147
msgid "A build that fails for any reason leaves the previous output, and the records of what it built, as they were. We fix the problem and build again."
msgstr "无论因何失败，构建都会让之前的输出及其构建记录保持原样。我们修复问题后重新构建即可。"
